# BP Dumper Versioning is Automated

BP Dumper versions are cut by **semantic-release** on pushes to `main`
(`release.config.js` + `.github/workflows/release-dumper.yml`). It computes the
next version from Conventional Commit messages, runs `sync-dumper-version.mjs`,
updates the changelog, tags `vX.Y.Z`, and triggers `build-releases.yml` to build
the exe.

## Never do these by hand

- Do **not** run `node scripts/sync-dumper-version.mjs <version>`.
- Do **not** edit version/manifest files — semantic-release owns them:
  - `scripts/bp-dumper/version.json`, `scripts/bp-dumper/package.json`
  - `scripts/bp-dumper-py/_version.py`, `scripts/bp-dumper-py/_min_game_version.py`
 - `scripts/bp-dumper-go/version.txt`, `scripts/bp-dumper-go/mingame.txt`
  - `src/data/bp-dumper-version.json`
  - `scripts/bp-dumper/CHANGELOG.md`
- Do **not** create git tags or trigger the build workflow manually.

## How to ship a dumper change

Commit dumper changes with a Conventional Commit **scoped to `dumper`**:

| Message | Release |
|---|---|
| `fix(dumper): ...` | patch |
| `feat(dumper): ...` | minor |
| `perf(dumper): ...` / `refactor(dumper): ...` | patch |
| `feat(dumper)!: ...` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer | major |

- A release is cut **only** when files under the dumper paths change (see the
  workflow `paths:`) **and** a `dumper`-scoped commit is present. Other scopes
  cut no dumper release.
- Keep dumper logic changes and unrelated site changes in separate commits so
  the scope stays accurate.
- In `release.config.js`, do **not** add a bare `{ release: false }` catch-all —
  it matches every commit and suppresses all bumps (including `feat(dumper)`).

## Every game patch cuts a dumper release

Ship a new dumper build on **every** game patch, even when no blueprints changed.

`MIN_GAME_VERSION` is the **recent-import** floor only (`IMPORT_OLD_LOGS` / first-run backup prompt). Patch-day bake sets it to current **major.minor** (e.g. `4.10`) so that prompt accepts **4.10.x** logs and skips older patches. It does **not** gate live watch, full history, or one-shot directory scans.

- Live watch tails `Game.log` with no min-version check.
- Full history (`FULL_HISTORY_IMPORT` / `--full-history-import`) always scans with the version filter **off**. Wizard Enter default is always **Y** (first launch and `--configure`); after it runs, the flag is written `false` so later launches do not rescan.
- One-shot / `--no-watch` directory scans of logbackups are backlog reads — no recent-import filter.
- The patch-day PR must include a **`dumper`-scoped** commit (e.g.
  `fix(dumper): rebuild for 4.10`). Data-only commits cut nothing.
- `release-dumper.yml` watches `src/data/game-build-version.json` and
  `src/data/blueprint-name-lookup.json`, so refreshed game data fires the workflow.
- `MIN_GAME_VERSION` is baked automatically: `prepareCmd` chains
  `syncDumperMinGameVersion.mjs`, which reads `game-build-version.json`. Never hand-run
  `npm run sync-min-game-version`.
- `build-releases.yml` runs `copy-blueprint-lookup` before building, so new blueprint
  names reach the exe and the `log-watcher-webhook` Edge Function without manual steps.
